{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Explanation","title":"Explanation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/DesignPrinciples"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swidux’s plugin system is a single protocol ("},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxPlugin","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":") with four lifecycle hooks and an ordered registry ("},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost","type":"reference"},{"text":"). All store extensibility flows through this contract. The built-in ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin"},{"text":" use it, and so do domain-specific features like killswitch enforcement and paywall management.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"The Dispatch Lifecycle","anchor":"The-Dispatch-Lifecycle","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Every call to ","type":"text"},{"code":"store.send()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" drives plugins through a four-phase lifecycle:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":null,"code":["plugins.willReduce(state:action:)      \/\/ 1. Pre-reduce (read-only state)","appReducer.reduce(state:action:...)    \/\/ 2. App reducer runs","pluginEffects = plugins.reduce(...)    \/\/ 3. Plugin reducers run","plugins.afterReduce(state:action:)     \/\/ 4. Post-reduce cleanup"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The generic ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store"},{"type":"text","text":" implements this lifecycle internally. You don’t write "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"send()"},{"text":" by hand — ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store.send()"},{"text":" handles packing, reducing, plugin hooks, unpacking, and effect dispatch.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A fifth method, ","type":"text"},{"code":"flush()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", runs once at shutdown to drain async buffers.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"All four hooks have default no-op implementations. Each plugin overrides only what it needs.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Core-Middleware-vs-Domain-Plugins","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Core Middleware vs Domain Plugins"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The plugin system serves two structurally different roles. Recognizing which one a plugin fills determines where it lives, which hooks it uses, and how it couples to the host app.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Core Middleware","anchor":"Core-Middleware","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin"},{"text":" are ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"action-agnostic infrastructure"}]},{"text":". They never inspect the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Action"},{"text":" type, never dispatch actions, and never return effects. They couple only to the shape of state:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" needs keypaths to "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" properties."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","type":"reference"},{"text":" needs ","type":"text"},{"code":"State: Equatable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" so it can snapshot and compare."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Because they don’t touch actions, they work with any app that uses Swidux — no wiring required beyond construction."}]},{"level":3,"text":"Domain Plugins","anchor":"Domain-Plugins","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Killswitch, parental gate, and paywall plugins are "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"domain-specific modules","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" that ship as separate library targets ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxKillswitch"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxParentalGate"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPaywall"},{"type":"text","text":"). They own their own state slices and action enums, dispatch effects, and must be explicitly wired into the host app’s root types."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each domain plugin stores three wiring pieces:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["private let stateKeyPath: WritableKeyPath<RootState, FeatureState>","private let toRootAction: @Sendable (FeatureAction) -> RootAction","private let extractAction: @Sendable (RootAction) -> FeatureAction?"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The host app provides these at init — the plugin never assumes a specific root type."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"Comparison","anchor":"Comparison","type":"heading"},{"header":"row","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Core Middleware"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Domain Plugins"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Action knowledge"}]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"None"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Full — extracts and lifts actions"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Lifecycle hooks"}]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce"},{"type":"text","text":" only"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Returns effects"}]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"State coupling"}]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keypath to "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"type":"text","text":" constraint"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keypath to plugin’s own state slice"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Wiring"}]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Construction only"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keypath + action lifter + action extractor"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Target"}]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Core "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Swidux"},{"type":"text","text":" library"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Separate library target"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Opt-in"}]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Instantiate and register"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add state, action case, and register"}]}]]],"type":"table"},{"level":2,"text":"The Decision Rule","anchor":"The-Decision-Rule","type":"heading"},{"style":"important","name":"Important","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Does the middleware need to know your action type? If "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"no"}]},{"type":"text","text":", it’s core middleware — put it in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Swidux"},{"type":"text","text":" and use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"},{"type":"text","text":". If "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"yes"}]},{"type":"text","text":", it’s a domain plugin — give it its own target and use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}],"type":"aside"},{"level":2,"text":"Hook Selection Guide","anchor":"Hook-Selection-Guide","type":"heading"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce(state:action:)"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — Capture state "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"before","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" the reducer mutates it. State is read-only. Use for snapshots (undo) or pre-mutation analytics."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce(state:action:) -> Effect?"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — Handle domain-specific actions "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"after","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" the app reducer. Mutate the plugin’s state slice and return effects. This is the only hook that can dispatch actions or do async work."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce(state:action:)"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — Observe state "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"after","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" all reducing is done. Use for persistence draining, logging, or metrics. Cannot return effects."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flush() async"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — Shutdown hook. Flush pending async buffers (persistence writes, analytics batches). Called once when the app exits."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"level":2,"text":"Registration Order","anchor":"Registration-Order","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" executes plugins in registration order. Recommended ordering:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let plugins = PluginHost<AppState, AppAction>()","plugins.register(undoPlugin)         \/\/ 1. Must snapshot before any mutation","plugins.register(persistencePlugin)  \/\/ 2. Drains changelogs after reducer","plugins.register(killswitchPlugin)   \/\/ 3. Domain plugins in any order","plugins.register(paywallPlugin)"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Undo must come first — it snapshots state in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce"},{"type":"text","text":", before the app reducer or any plugin modifies it. Persistence typically comes next so its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"},{"type":"text","text":" drain sees the final state. Domain plugins use only "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce"},{"type":"text","text":", so their relative order rarely matters."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Service-Result Actions and Transition Observation","anchor":"Service-Result-Actions-and-Transition-Observation","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"service-result action"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":"’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"customerInfoUpdated"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"KillswitchPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":"’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"verdictReceived"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FeatureFlagsPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":"’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refreshSucceeded"},{"type":"text","text":" — fires on "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"every"}]},{"type":"text","text":" fetch, refresh, or stream tick, not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"only when the value changed, and unconditionally writes its payload to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"state slice. The payload is frequently identical to what is already there"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(a re-delivered entitlement, an unchanged remote config)."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Do "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"not"}]},{"type":"text","text":" map analytics or side effects to the raw service-result action:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it fires duplicates by design. Observe the "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"state slice"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — or a value"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"derived from it — instead."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"State observation is already deduplicated by the framework. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store.send"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"packs the observer into a value-type snapshot, lets reducers mutate the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"snapshot, then writes back via "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"State.apply"},{"type":"text","text":". For a leaf slice that write"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is a plain assignment whose "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"type":"text","text":" setter equality-gates "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"values, so a slice whose value did not change emits no notification — and a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"value-diffing consumer such as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsIdentity.userProperties"},{"type":"text","text":" (which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" re-evaluates and diffs every non-analytics dispatch) sees exactly the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"real transitions. This dedup is a property of the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store"},{"type":"text","text":", not of any"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"per-plugin guard, so a no-op service-result cycle is silent to state"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"observers without any extra reducer logic.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Next Steps","type":"heading","anchor":"Next-Steps","level":2},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" — Step-by-step guide to creating a domain plugin","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" — Configure the built-in persistence middleware"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" — Add undo\/redo with the built-in undo middleware","type":"text"}]}]}]}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Extend the dispatch cycle with lifecycle hooks — from invisible infrastructure to domain-specific features."}],"kind":"article","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture"},"sections":[],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Plugin Architecture","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"role":"article"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginarchitecture"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoRedo":{"role":"article","title":"Undo \/ Redo","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Add stack-based undo\/redo to your app with "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoredo","type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistencePlugin":{"role":"symbol","title":"PersistencePlugin","abstract":[{"text":"Coalescing persistence plugin.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"PersistencePlugin"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"PersistencePlugin"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistenceplugin","type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"role":"collection","title":"Swidux","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates."}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","url":"\/documentation\/swidux","type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/EntityStore":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystore","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An ordered, keyed collection of identifiable entities that silently records"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every mutation for downstream persistence."}],"title":"EntityStore","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityStore"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityStore"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide":{"role":"article","title":"Persistence Middleware","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Configure automatic persistence that drains entity changes and batches database writes."}],"kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistencemiddlewareguide","type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginHost":{"title":"PluginHost","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"PluginHost"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Ordered registry of plugins that drives the dispatch lifecycle."}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"PluginHost"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginhost"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/SwiduxPlugin":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/swiduxplugin","title":"SwiduxPlugin","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SwiduxPlugin"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxPlugin","abstract":[{"text":"A plugin that participates in the Swidux dispatch cycle.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SwiduxPlugin"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/ArchitectureGuide":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/architectureguide","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Understand the architectural patterns that make Swidux work correctly with SwiftUI’s observation system."}],"title":"Architecture & Performance","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","type":"topic","role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/BuildingADomainPlugin":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/buildingadomainplugin","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Create a self-contained feature plugin with its own state, actions, and effects."}],"title":"Building a Domain Plugin","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","type":"topic","role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoPlugin":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoplugin","title":"UndoPlugin","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Snapshot-based undo\/redo plugin."}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"UndoPlugin"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"UndoPlugin"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/DesignPrinciples":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/designprinciples","role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The 10 rules that shape every Swidux app, and the reasoning behind them."}],"kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/DesignPrinciples","title":"Design Principles"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Store":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/store","title":"Store","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Store","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Generic store that owns the dispatch cycle, plugin lifecycle, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"observation layer."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Store","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic"}}}